          <caption>
            <p>Sleep Polygraph, 120-Second Window. The polygraph, recorded during sleep, shows electroencephalogram, electrooculogram, electrocardiogram, and chin electromyogram during a 120-second window. Note the repetitive obstructive apnea with persistent effort during cessation of both flow channels (nasal pressure flow and thermistor) followed by desaturation (light blue arrows) and arousals (dark blue arrows). Contributed by A Sankari, MD, PhD</p>
